      "marks": 5,
      "answer": "$4x+y-2z=8$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "EITHER: Use a scalar product to obtain a relevant equation in $a,b,c$, e.g. $a+2b+3c=0$ — B1. Obtain a second relevant equation, e.g. using $\\overrightarrow{PA}$, $a+4b+4c=0$, and solve for one ratio — M1. Obtain $a:b:c=4:1:-2$ — A1. Substitute a relevant point and find $d$ — M1. Obtain $4x+y-2z=8$, or equivalent — A1. OR1: Attempt $(\\mathbf i+4\\mathbf j+4\\mathbf k)\\times(\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+3\\mathbf k)$ — M1. Obtain two correct components — A1. Obtain $4\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j-2\\mathbf k$ — A1. Substitute a relevant point and find $d$ — M1. Obtain $4x+y-2z=8$ — A1. OR2: Form a relevant 2-parameter plane equation — M1. State $\\mathbf r=4\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+5\\mathbf k+\\lambda(\\mathbf i+4\\mathbf j+4\\mathbf k)+\\mu(\\mathbf i+2\\mathbf j+3\\mathbf k)$ — A1. State three correct component equations — A1. Eliminate $\\lambda,\\mu$ — M1. Obtain $4x+y-2z=8$ — A1. Total: 5.",
